## The maze

The maze in @fig-maze has 27 free cells. The agent moves north, east, south or west into a free cell; walls and the border block movement. Every move earns $-1$, entering the goal earns $+10$ more, and the goal ends the episode. So from a cell $\delta$ moves from the goal, the best return is $10 - \delta$: reaching the goal is always worth it, and shorter is better.

Formally, a search problem has a state space $\mathcal{S}$, the valid actions $\mathcal{A}(s)$ in each state (none in an absorbing state such as the goal), a deterministic transition $T(s, a)$ giving the next state, and a reward $R(s, a)$.

